{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> \"Therefore you and your entire congregation have gathered together\" — that you assemble against HaShem. The meaning is like \"the rulers take counsel together against YHWH and against His anointed\" (Psalms 2:2) — they made an assembly to contend with HaShem. Likewise, \"when they rebelled against YHWH\" (Deuteronomy 1:43). And some say that the heh of נועדים is superfluous." "<b>What has he.</b> What is his transgression — what is he doing?"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Resolved וי\"א as 'and some say'; the reference is to the heh prefix in the word נועדים from the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:58.699399888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}